Benjamin Scott-Hopkins wrote:
> I think I know how prayer works (read the FAQ, searched here, &c.) but
> I want to make sure about a few things. Essentially, all that matters
> (if you want favors) is positive luck and positive alignment, right?
> Neither have to be _super_ high, do they? Here's four questions:

Here's how praying for gifts works:

NetHack generates a random number in [0, (luck+6)/2).
0: Nothing
1: fixes/blesses weapon
2: Golden glow (+5 max HP)
3: Hint (or golden glow)
4: Remove curse
5: Protection (or an intrinsic)
6: Spellbook
7-9: Crowning (or spellbook)

Unfortunately, crowning means you can pray *much* less than you could otherwise,
so it's nice to avoid it. For that to happen, you want a number in [0,7) -->
(luck+6)/2=7 --> luck E {8,9}. That's a very awkward number to get. The best
method would probably be to max out your luck and carry an uncursed luckstone,
then smash a mirror. When praying, put away all your blessed luckstones (which
would make your luck 11).

That's possibly more trouble than it's worth. Being crowned increases your
chance of getting spellbooks when your luck is maxed out - 1/3 (plus 1/9
protection plus 2/9 golden glow), versus 1/7 (plus 1/7 protection plus 2/7
golden glow) if you're dodging crowning. Of course, the difference in prayer
timeouts when crowned is much larger than a factor of 7/3, so you will get less
this way.

